# Portfolio assistant ("Ask about me").
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the key. `.env.local` is gitignored
# — never commit a real key, and never rename this to a NEXT_PUBLIC_* variable:
# that prefix ships the value to the browser.
#
# Used only by src/app/api/chat/route.ts, which runs on the server.
#
# Free key, no card needed: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Only set this if the default model stops working — Google retires
# models on its own schedule and returns 404 "no longer available to new users".
#
# Listing models is NOT a reliable check: it advertises models your key may not
# be allowed to call. Test the model itself:
#
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w "%{http_code}\n" \
#     -X POST "https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/MODEL_NAME:generateContent" \
#     -H "content-type: application/json" -H "x-goog-api-key: YOUR_KEY" \
#     -d '{"contents":[{"role":"user","parts":[{"text":"hi"}]}]}'
#
# 200 means usable. Or set gemini-flash-lite-latest, which never 404s but lets
# Google change the model under you.
#
# Check the DAILY quota before moving to a bigger model. The free tier caps
# gemini-3.6-flash at 20 requests a day for the entire site — roughly twenty
# visitor questions and the assistant is finished until tomorrow. The lite
# models are the ones with a quota a public page can actually run on.
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.1-flash-lite
